# Category card image darkness

## Re-learned 2026-09-16

Owner: Category Management previews look dark. **Cause = intentional dark overlay**, not a dim source file.

### Admin — Category Management

In `CategoryManager.tsx` preview tile:

```tsx
<div className="absolute inset-0 bg-black/20"></div>
```

20% black over the background image so white emoji/title/description stay readable in the admin list.

### Storefront homepage

Category cards use a readability scrim (owner: keep photos visible, not muddy):

```tsx
bg-gradient-to-t from-black/28 via-black/10 to-transparent
```

**2026-09-16:** Lightened stepwise `/75`→`/55`→`/40`→`/28` so customers see brighter category images. Soft base remains for white copy. Do not jump back to `/75` without owner OK.

Admin Category Management preview stays at `bg-black/20` (list UI only).

### Do / don’t

- Do: explain overlay first if owner says “image is dark.”
- Do not: strip admin `/20` or home gradient without owner OK (text contrast regresses).
- Do not: confuse with hero title rule (hero = no fill panel; category cards may keep scrims).
